From 07b9d2f9bca4f6756d61ee35519126060ae72e99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:56:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): refuse a Face whose 'Do not touch' keep-out blocks a
 level

A keep-out covers the heights from its level up to the clearance plane,
so the blocked levels are always the lowest. A blocked level left the
whole face above Cut Z, and only a note said so. A toolpath has no
"incomplete" state, so the Face is now refused by name. The refusal
gives Cut Z and the depth that the face reaches, and names the fixes.

Pinned by face_keep::a_keepout_that_blocks_the_lower_levels_refuses_with_the_depth_reached.

Fixes #3526

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
